course: dictionary
lesson: 13552
title: Improperly: the wrong way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Improperly is an adverb. It tells you how something was done, and it means in a wrong or incorrect way, not as it should be done. Look at the parts: im- means not, proper means right and correct, so improperly means done in a not-right way.
explain: «The shelf was improperly fixed, so it fell down.» The clue is fell down. A shelf that falls was not fixed the right way. Try your meaning in the sentence: the shelf was fixed in a wrong way, so it fell. It still makes sense.
explain: Improperly can also mean not polite, honest or allowed. «The boy behaved improperly in class and was asked to leave.» The words asked to leave show he broke the rules. Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: Improperly means in a wrong or incorrect way.
fact: Improperly can also mean in a way that is not polite, honest or allowed.
fact: The root word is proper, which means right and correct. The prefix im- turns it into the opposite.
fact: «Improperly dressed» means wearing the wrong clothes for the time or place.
fact: A good check is to swap in "in a wrong way" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The shelf was improperly fixed, so it fell down.» What does improperly mean here? | In a very quick way | In a loud way | *In a wrong way, not as it should be done | In a happy way
exercise: «The boy behaved improperly in class.» What does improperly suggest? | He sang a song for the whole class | *He did not act politely or as he was allowed to | He won a prize for his work | He was very tired after lunch
exercise: Which word means the opposite of improperly, in a right and correct way? | *Properly | Loudly | Slowly | Sadly
test: «She was improperly dressed for the snow in only a thin T-shirt.» What does improperly dressed mean? | Wearing brand new shoes | Wearing a costume to a party | *Wearing the wrong clothes for the weather | Wearing very bright colours
test: Which sentence shows someone breaking the rules? | The dog ran improperly fast across the park | *She acted improperly and took the sweets without asking | The sun rose improperly early
exam: Pick the best meaning of «improperly» in «The tool was improperly used, so it broke.» | *In a wrong way, not as it should be used | In a careful, gentle way | In a fast and clever way | In a kind and honest way
